WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:05.160
If you're a superhero fan, 2018 already looks
to be an exciting year.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.250
Movies featuring Black Panther, the Flash,
and Aquaman are all scheduled, and there's

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.390
also a little movie called Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:19.619
But one 2018 release is absolutely guaranteed
to to rock your world: Deadpool 2.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:23.960
The Merc With a Mouth is returning with several
fan favorites from the first movie — and

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.699
the cinematic debut of some more classic comic
book characters.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:32.660
We've got two crisp high-fives worth of reasons
Deadpool 2 will blow everyone away.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.559
"OK guys lets get out there and make a difference."

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:38.940
"(you know what to do)"

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.729
John Wick approved

00:00:40.729 --> 00:00:46.579
If you want to get someone excited about Deadpool
2, you only need to use two words: John Wick.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:51.089
After some behind-the-scenes drama that caused
Deadpool director Tim Miller to bail on the

00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:54.389
sequel, the project landed David Leitch to
take up the job.

00:00:54.389 --> 00:01:00.100
Leitch injected fresh energy into the action
genre with the first John Wick, taking a tired

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.049
revenge premise and building it into something
completely awesome.

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:08.820
If Leitch can marry the sleek, stylish action
of John Wick with the crude, off-the-wall

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.830
humor of Deadpool, he'll create a superhero
movie like nothing we've seen.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.720
Or at least a worthy successor.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.010
Sequel skewering

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.570
It wouldn't be Deadpool if it didn't poke
fun at itself, and a Deadpool sequel is bound

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.090
to go the same way.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.480
As excited as fans get about the return of
their favorite heroes and villains, too often

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.390
the sequels just lack the spark that made
the originals so good.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:37.210
Fortunately, Deadpool 2 is setting out to
put unnecessary super-sequels in their place.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.100
As producer Simon Kinberg put it,

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.600
"The sort of glut or saturation of these movies
and the proliferation of sequels is definitely

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.570
something we'll play around with."

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:50.410
Even your reluctant friend who can't stand
each year's endless superhero sequels and

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:56.630
reboots might get a kick out of this phenomenon
being brutally savaged by Deadpool's sarcasm.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.370
Deadpool and friends

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:02.090
Deadpool 2 will be expanding its roster of
characters by at least two.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:07.390
One will be Domino, a mutant with a very special
ability that can only be described as "good

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.390
luck."

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:11.409
When she wants something to happen, she can
greatly increase the odds.

00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:15.390
In the comics, she's had several run-ins with
Deadpool, though their exact relationship

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.989
in the upcoming sequel remains unclear.

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:21.909
In addition to potentially bringing Domino,
to life on the big screen, the movie will

00:02:21.909 --> 00:02:25.819
also likely fulfill its promise from the end
of the first one:

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:27.250
"The sequel?

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.489
We're gonna have Cable.

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:29.569
Amazing character.

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:30.650
Bionic arm.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.650
Time Travel."

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.549
In the comics, Cable has a pretty complex
backstory involving time travel and a weird

00:02:35.549 --> 00:02:41.010
techno-organic virus, a mashup of time paradoxes
and clones that any movie studio would have

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.269
a hard time translating to the screen.

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:46.120
Basically, a standalone Cable movie ain't
gonna happen.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:51.120
But if Deadpool 2 got ahold of him, Cable
doesn't have to be anything but a badass,

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.810
bullet-slinging future-warrior — the guy
we all want to see — and be right at home

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.159
in Deadpool's bonkers cinematic world.

00:02:58.159 --> 00:03:02.939
Look no further than the Deadpool video game
for proof of their perfect double act:

00:03:02.939 --> 00:03:05.950
"This has got to be the dumbest idea you've
ever had.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.739
The risk is considerable.

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:09.739
This is my..."

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.900
"Great Cable, awesome thanks, see ya, goodbye!"

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.090
Hello X-Force

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:19.779
To casual fans, some of these new additions
to the Deadpool sequel may seem a little random.

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:24.560
After all, a time-traveling cyborg and lady
luck seem out of place in the somewhat grounded

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.150
reality of Deadpool's corner of the X-Men
cinematic universe.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.049
But as with all things Hollywood, there are
bigger things on the horizon.

00:03:32.049 --> 00:03:35.670
In 20th Century Fox's case, that means an
X-Force film.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:41.139
In the comics, the X-Force was formed by Cable
as a mutant team that specialized in "wetwork"

00:03:41.139 --> 00:03:44.389
— a fancy way of saying hacking up bad guys.

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:48.940
The initial lineup featured Cable as the leader
and Domino as one of his ace soldiers, and

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.769
now both of these characters are slated to
be in Deadpool 2.

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:57.669
And with Ryan Reynolds reportedly co-writing
the X-Force script, chances are good that

00:03:57.669 --> 00:04:01.819
Deadpool 2 will start laying the foundation
for the X-Force.

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:02.959
Returning favorites

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:07.489
It's not all new names and faces for Deadpool
2 — all the best parts of the first movie

00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:08.749
are coming back, too.

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:13.139
So far, the sequel is confirmed to feature
Deadpool's main squeeze Vanessa, Negasonic

00:04:13.139 --> 00:04:18.540
Teenage Warhead, Colossus, and our favorite
taxi driver since Robert De Niro: Dopinder.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.709
"Dopinder, this is no way to win Geeta's heart
back.

00:04:21.709 --> 00:04:22.930
(I'm so proud of you)."

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:26.150
There's also a chance that Vanessa will play
a bigger role in the action.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:31.230
In the comics, the character Vanessa is based
on is a mutant with the codename Copycat,

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:35.410
who has the ability to steal the appearance
and powers of other characters.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:39.280
More likely, though, Deadpool's just gonna
stick Vanessa in a flashy outfit and make

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.670
a joke about it.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.690
Yeah, that's more Wade's style.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.000
More superhero mockery

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.850
For better or worse, we're swimming in superhero
movies for the foreseeable future.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:54.150
From Warner Bros. establishing their own cinematic
universe to the unending march of the MCU,

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:58.120
it seems like there's always a cape, web,
or magic hammer hanging out at your local

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.120
movie theater.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:04.250
One of the things that made Deadpool so funny
was the way it relentlessly lampooned these

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:09.180
other superhero movies, from the opening credits
to Deadpool's breakdown of Angel's "superhero

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.180
landing."

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.480
"Superhero landing.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.300
You know that's really hard on your knees.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.460
It's really impracticable, they all do it."

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:19.720
And, of course, the meta-mockery of Reynolds'
failed Green Lantern movie.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:23.070
"Please don't make the super-suit green!

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.410
Or animated!"

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:29.740
One simple reason to be excited about Deadpool
2 is that there are so many more movies for

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.740
it to make fun of.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:35.150
Since Deadpool, we've seen Logan, Captain
America: Civil War, Batman v Superman, Doctor

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.900
Strange, and Suicide Squad.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:41.830
And by the time Deadpool 2 comes out Spider-Man:
Homecoming will have been released, as well

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.050
as Guardians of the Galaxy Volume 2.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:49.220
If Deadpool's gonna pick at superheroes like
we know he will, he's got plenty of material

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.090
to work with this time around.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.650
Low-budget creativity

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:57.260
With all of Deadpool's gorgeous visuals and
slo-mo sarcasm, you might be surprised that

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:01.070
it was made with a budget of only $58 million.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:05.950
In the world of superhero cinema, where bloated
films like Batman v Superman clock in at budgets

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:11.370
of $250 million and beyond, Deadpool was essentially
made for chump change.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:15.740
This forced the creative team to put an emphasis
on characters, relationships, and humor.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.650
Deadpool 2 co-writer Paul Wernick has insisted
the sequel will also be relatively cheap,

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.650
saying,

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:26.170
"We don't want $150 million to go make the
next movie, because that's not Deadpool.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:30.320
Deadpool doesn't lift cities up into the air
or battle aliens coming down to earth."

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:34.970
Taking this interview at face value, it means
the sequel will see a continued focus on humor,

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:39.480
relationships, and comparatively low-stakes
action — great news for those of us who

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.800
really appreciated the character-driven original.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.290
That amazing trailer

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:49.060
If you saw Logan in theaters, you were treated
to a doozie of a teaser — the Deadpool 2

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:52.920
promo that disguised itself as the beginning
of the Logan movie.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:57.840
Based on that alone, you can bet Deadpool
2 is going to blow us all away, with references

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.630
to Cable's real name and the best Stan Lee
cameo yet.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.640
"Wow, nice suit."

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.340
"Zip it Stan Lee!"

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:10.970
It's a solid assurance that the original's
violence, humor, and self-deprecating humor

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.320
remain in force.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.740
Also, what's up with that Firefly poster?

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.970
Just a nod to Vanessa actress Morena Baccarin?

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:19.180
A jab at Fox for canceling the show?

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.190
With Deadpool, it could mean anything...or
nothing.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:26.080
All we know right now is that Deadpool 2 is
going to be amazing.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.080
How amazing?

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.750
"I'm touching myself tonight."

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:29.750
Thanks for watching!

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:32.310
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:34.750
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

